{
  "description": "The -alis/-aris adjectives of Jacobs (2026), with the paper's underlying forms, in which [lateral] is specified only on liquids and the suffix is /-alis/, and its classification of each form. Segments are phonemic: c is [k], consonantal v is [w], and the e of ae and oe is [j] (Cser 2020, Figure 1).",
  "Types": {
    "Status": [
      {"Value": "regular", "Lean": "regular", "Description": "a form the paper's account derives"},
      {"Value": "glide", "Lean": "glide", "Description": "a later -alis form the paper derives from a [j] formed from a front vowel in hiatus"},
      {"Value": "exception", "Lean": "exception", "Description": "a form the paper calls an exception"},
      {"Value": "unexplained", "Lean": "unexplained", "Description": "a form the paper reports without accounting for it"}
    ]
  },
